From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jean-Michael Celerier <jmcelerier@sat.qc.ca>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:30:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] SPIRV-Cross: GLSL: cast gl_ViewID_OVR to int when loading
 ViewIndex

SPIR-V's ViewIndex builtin is a signed int, as is Vulkan GLSL's
gl_ViewIndex, but GL_OVR_multiview declares gl_ViewID_OVR as
"in highp uint". The GLSL backend substitutes the name and loads it
with no cast, so a shader that stores the view index into an int --
`v_face = gl_ViewIndex;` -- becomes `v_face = gl_ViewID_OVR;`, which
GLSL forbids:

    error C7011: implicit cast from "uint" to "int"   (NVIDIA)
    'assign' : cannot convert from 'in uint ViewIndex' to 'flat out int'
                                                      (glslang)

Handle ViewIndex in cast_from_variable_load like the other builtins
whose GLSL type differs from SPIR-V's: when not targeting Vulkan
semantics, the loaded value is a uint, and bitcast_expression wraps it
as int(gl_ViewID_OVR). Uses that need a uint get uint(int(...)), which
is exact for view indices. The HLSL backend goes through the same path
and gets int(gl_ViewIndex) from its uint SV_ViewID, which it already
accepted implicitly. MSL has its own cast_from_variable_load.

Not in upstream SPIRV-Cross main as of 2026-10-11.
---
 src/3rdparty/SPIRV-Cross/spirv_glsl.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/SPIRV-Cross/spirv_glsl.cpp b/src/3rdparty/SPIRV-Cross/spirv_glsl.cpp
index f9b489c..aab14c8 100644
--- a/src/3rdparty/SPIRV-Cross/spirv_glsl.cpp
+++ b/src/3rdparty/SPIRV-Cross/spirv_glsl.cpp
@@ -19682,6 +19682,17 @@ void CompilerGLSL::cast_from_variable_load(uint32_t source_id, std::string &expr
 		expected_type = SPIRType::UInt;
 		break;
 
+	case BuiltInViewIndex:
+		// SPIR-V's ViewIndex is a signed int, and so is Vulkan GLSL's
+		// gl_ViewIndex, but GL_OVR_multiview declares gl_ViewID_OVR as
+		// "in highp uint" (and HLSL's SV_ViewID is uint too). Without a cast,
+		// storing the view index into an int is an implicit uint -> int
+		// conversion, which GLSL forbids:
+		//   error C7011: implicit cast from "uint" to "int"
+		if (!options.vulkan_semantics)
+			expected_type = SPIRType::UInt;
+		break;
+
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
